Stage 5: the content sets on R14 baselines.

commit:    28941070945cc37c6d4784598502b11871944514
machine:   4 vCPU Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.80GHz, 15 GiB, 6.18.44-fc-v37
sdk:       8.0.131; Google.Protobuf 3.28.3, Grpc.Tools 2.66.0

R7 CONFIGURATION, INCLUDING THE MARSHALLER PATH (R14).

The headline baseline is the codec path ArmoniK RUNS, not the library's
fastest entry point. Grpc.Tools emits into the stub:
    context.SetPayloadLength(message.CalculateSize());
    MessageExtensions.WriteTo(message, context.GetBufferWriter());
and decodes with parser.ParseFrom(context.PayloadAsReadOnlySequence()).
packages/csharp calls no message serialisation directly; the two
ToByteArray() hits there are ByteString, copying a data chunk.

  encode baseline  gp-marshaller   CalculateSize + WriteTo(IBufferWriter)
  decode baseline  gp-parse-seq    ParseFrom(ReadOnlySequence), 1 segment
  second rows      gp-writeto / gp-parse   the SPAN forms
                   gp-bufferwriter         no size pass: the library's best,
                                           which no ArmoniK process runs
                   gp-parse-seg            sequence segmented at 16 KB, which
                                           is what a 540 KB response arrives as
                   gp-tobytearray          what application code would write

LOOP SHAPE (R14). A message is serialised once in production, so a loop over
one instance is only valid if the library memoises nothing per instance.
CHECKED, not assumed: Google.Protobuf's C# backend emits no _memoizedSize
field and CalculateSize() recomputes from scratch on every call, unlike
protobuf-java. So this loop amortises nothing.

